      "text": "Pangasinan Fare Reference  cleaned edition\nPage 4\n2. TRICYCLE — PANGASINAN LGU-BASED FARES\nImportant: Pangasinan does not have one province-wide tricycle fare per kilometer. Motorized tricycle fares are prescribed by the relevant city or\nmunicipality. Official provincial records show separate local ordinances for different LGUs.\nLatest verified Pangasinan example with an explicit per-km formula\nDagupan City — Ordinance No. 2355-2025. This is a Dagupan City rate only, not a province-wide rate.\n Distance\nShared / regular\nSpecial  1 passenger\nSpecial  2 passengers\nSpecial  3–4 passengers\n1 km\n■20\n■30\n■50\n■60\n2 km\n■20\n■30\n■50\n■60\n3 km\n■30\n■40\n■60\n■70\n4 km\n■40\n■50\n■70\n■80\n5 km\n■50\n■60\n■80\n■90\n6 km\n■60\n■70\n■90\n■100\n7 km\n■70\n■80\n■100\n■110\n8 km\n■80\n■90\n■110\n■120\n9 km\n■90\n■100\n■120\n■130\n10 km\n■100\n■110\n■130\n■140\n11 km\n■110\n■120\n■140\n■150\n12 km\n■120\n■130\n■150\n■160\n13 km\n■130\n■140\n■160\n■170\n14 km\n■140\n■150\n■170\n■180\n15 km\n■150\n■160\n■180\n■190\n16 km\n■160\n■170\n■190\n■200\n17 km\n■170\n■180\n■200\n■210\n18 km\n■180\n■190\n■210\n■220\n19 km\n■190\n■200\n■220\n■230\n20 km\n■200\n■210\n■230\n■240\nDagupan formula: Shared/non-holding-area ride = ■20 per passenger for the first 2 km + ■10 for every succeeding kilometer. Special hire = ■30 for 1 passenger,\n■25 each for 2 passengers, or ■20 each for 3–4 passengers for the first 2 km, plus ■10 for every succeeding kilometer. Senior citizens, PWDs and students receive\n20% off the computed fare with valid ID. Optional night differential: up to 10% from 9:00 p.m. to 5:00 a.m.\nLGU\nLatest local ordinance identified\nSource establishes\nDagupan City\nOrdinance 2355-2025\nNew tricycle fare matrix; explicit per-km formula\nAlcala\nMunicipal Ordinance 2026-03\nUpdated fare matrix; Provincial Resolution 840-2026\nBautista\nMunicipal Ordinance 04, s-2025\nUpdated fare matrix; Provincial Resolution 575-2025\nSual\nMunicipal Ordinance 04-2024\nNew fare rates; Provincial Resolution 8-2025\nAI/data-use rule: For a tricycle route inside Pangasinan, use the fare ordinance of the municipality/city where the tricycle operates. Do not apply the Dagupan table to\nanother LGU unless that LGU adopts the same rate. If no current local fare matrix can be verified, mark the fare as not verified rather than inventing a provincial rate.\n",
